#{[17592186561047 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561047 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561047 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561047 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A=\\{n\\in N∣n+1\\ge 2\\}$ and $B=\\{n\\in Z∣n-1\\ge -2\\}?$\n\nI. $A⊆B$\n\nII. $∅⊈A$\n\nIII. $B⊈A$\n\nIV. $B⊇A$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561047 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ca4e5acb-c615-5b3e-863b-498834fef823" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561047 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $n+1\\ge 2,$ that is to say, $n\\ge 1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{1,2,3,4,5,6,…\\}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $n-1\\ge -2,$ That is to say, $n\\ge -1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB=\\{-1,0,1,2,3,4,5,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is true. Every element in the set $A$ is an element of the set $B.$\n\n- $∅⊈A$ is false. The null set $∅=\\{\\}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\n- $B⊈A$ is true. For example, $0\\in B$ but $0\\notin A.$\n\n- $B⊇A$ is equivalent to $A⊆B,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561055 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186560933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561055 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561055 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561055 #edb/ref 1071 "Which set is a subset of $A=\\{l,m,n\\}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561055 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e7899b45-120a-5ab1-97c8-2f3192dc7444" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186561055 #edb/ref 1074 "A set is a subset of $A$ if all its elements are elements of $A.$\n\nOf the given sets, only $\\{m\\}$ has all of its elements in $A.$\n\nTherefore, $\\{m\\}$ is a subset of $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
